Make the new-profile card fill its background area with the RozeLynx illustration.

Upstream .new-profile-card .profile-background-image pins background-size to
80px because assets/plus.svg is an 80x80 currentColor plus glyph. RozeLynx
overwrites that asset with the full "create a new profile" illustration, so the
80px pin now shrinks the whole scene. The sibling profile cards already use
"cover" (the .profile-background-image base rule), so match them.

Identical in Firefox 155 and 156.

--- a/browser/components/profiles/content/profile-card.css
+++ b/browser/components/profiles/content/profile-card.css
@@ -47,7 +47,14 @@
   }
 
   .profile-background-image {
-    background-size: 80px;
+    /* RozeLynx: assets/plus.svg is no longer the 80x80 currentColor plus
+     * glyph, it is the full "create a new profile" illustration wrapped in
+     * an SVG at the card's own aspect ratio (see the ebuild's
+     * rozelynx_install_vector_slot call for plus.svg and
+     * branding/PLACEHOLDERS.md). Size it the same way the sibling profile
+     * cards size their artwork so it fills the 136px background area
+     * instead of being downscaled to 80px. */
+    background-size: cover;
   }
 
   .profile-details {
